//? Title: DnCNN: explicit tensor residual denoising
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
An image corrupted by additive Gaussian noise should recover clean intensities without losing real structure. This example predicts signed noise and subtracts it,starting with hand residual/filter checks and the actual Gaussian stream. Full and compact17-layer graphs,real CIFAR previews,visible Adam and paired BN restoration make the short denoising fit reproducible.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/dncnn.cpp`.

> The method

For y=x+v,a convolutional residual predictor estimates v from y alone.
Its half-MSE objective supervises the actual rounded additive residual.
Orthogonal convolutions and moving batch normalization retain the source
17-layer connectivity. Every preprocessing,objective,inference and scoring
operation uses tensors;host containers carry only metadata,RNG draws and
plot presentation values.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/dncnn_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/dncnn_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/dncnn_concept.tikz > build/dncnn_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/dncnn_concept.svg build/dncnn_concept.dvi > build/dncnn_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
