> Full and compact17-layer graphs

The first3x3 convolution has the only convolution bias. Fifteen hidden
bias-free Conv/BN/ReLU stages follow;the last bias-free linear convolution
predicts noise. Flattened kernels use orthogonal initialization,with orthogonal
columns when fan-in permits and rows otherwise. BN epsilon is1e-4,old-state
retention.05(new-batch weight.95). Training moments use population variance;
saved moving variance uses the unbiased correction.
```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  std::print("| width | learned scalars | learned tensors | BN scalars/tensors | stages "
             "|\n|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|\n");
  for (int width : {64, 16}) {
    n::ParameterStore p(3), state(4);
    const auto x = (.5 + .7 * n::sin(n::arange(0, 2 * 19 * 21, 1, n::DType::Float64) * .17))
                       .to(n::DType::Float32)
                       .reshape({2, 19, 21, 1})
                       .requires_grad_();
    const auto target = (.1 * n::cos(n::arange(0, 2 * 19 * 21, 1, n::DType::Float64) * .13))
                            .to(n::DType::Float32)
                            .reshape({2, 19, 21, 1});
    const auto out = m::DnCNN(p, state, x, width, true, false);
    auto leaves = p.parameters();
    leaves.push_back(x);
    const auto gradients = n::grad(m::DnResidualLoss(out.noise, target), leaves);
    for (const auto &g : gradients)
      if (!n::all(n::less(n::abs(g), INFINITY)).item<bool>() ||
          n::sum(n::square(g.to(n::DType::Float64))).item() <= 0)
        return 1;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < out.stages.size(); ++i)
      if (out.stages[i].shape() != n::Shape{2, 19, 21, i == 16 ? 1 : width})
        return 1;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {}/{} | {} |\n", width, p.count(), p.size(), state.count(),
               state.size(), out.stages.size());
  }
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| width | learned scalars | learned tensors | BN scalars/tensors | stages |
|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|
| 64 | 556096 | 48 | 1920/30 | 17 |
| 16 | 35344 | 48 | 480/30 | 17 |
// result_end

> Actual natural images and observed corruption

CIFAR training rows0–255 fit the model;training256–287 form validation.
Official-test rows128–159 are held out. Convert original32px encoded RGB
to grayscale using.299R+.587G+.114B,then apply sigma25/255 AWGN. Validation
and test seeds43/47 remain fixed. The fitting probe uses seed41;training
uses fresh5300+epoch corruption. The existing official CIFAR cache follows
`DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR` or XDG/home dataset paths. Class labels are unused.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dncnn_inputs.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <numeric>
#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("cifar10", (cache / "cifar10").string());

  constexpr double sigma = 25. / 255;
  const auto raw =
                 n::data::LoadCifar({cache / "cifar10/data_batch_1.bin"}, n::data::Cifar::k10),
             testing =
                 n::data::LoadCifar({cache / "cifar10/test_batch.bin"}, n::data::Cifar::k10);
  std::vector<std::size_t> fi(256), vi(32), ti(32);
  std::iota(fi.begin(), fi.end(), 0);
  std::iota(vi.begin(), vi.end(), 256);
  std::iota(ti.begin(), ti.end(), 128);
  const auto clean = m::DnImages(raw.images, fi);
  const auto fixed = m::DnCorrupt(clean, sigma, 41),
             validation = m::DnCorrupt(m::DnImages(raw.images, vi), sigma, 43),
             test = m::DnCorrupt(m::DnImages(testing.images, ti), sigma, 47);

  const auto first = m::DnBatch(fixed, {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7});
  const auto box = m::DnBoxFilter(first.noisy);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(m::DnPreviewTiles(first, box, box), "build/dncnn_inputs.png", 1, 0, 1, 0,
                     0, 3);
  const auto score = m::ScoreTensorDn(test.noisy, test.clean);
  std::print(
      "Fit/validation/test {}/{}/{};sigma {:.8f};fixed test raw noisy PSNR {:.6f}dB,outside "
      "fraction {:.6f}.\nPreview rows:noisy|fixed box|box repeated|clean|4x red box error.\n",
      clean.size(0), validation.clean.size(0), test.clean.size(0), sigma, score.psnr.item(),
      score.outside.item());
}
```
